# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Arslan Mazitov et al. (2025). PET-MAD as a lightweight universal interatomic potential for advanced materials modeling.
#   Nature Communications. doi:10.1038/s41467-025-65662-7  arXiv:2503.14118v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2503.14118v2 (sha256 eb550550c4d60044...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 186 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the PET-MAD model (Point Edge Transformer trained on
# the MAD data set): reference calculations, data set, architecture and
# training settings, training cost, and its energy and force MAEs on the
# MAD splits and on six external benchmark sets (Table I). The comparison
# models of Table I, the fine-tuned and bespoke PET models and the six
# application studies are not encoded; see gaps. Read from the arXiv
# preprint (v2).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-mazitov2025 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Mazitov et al. (2025): PET-MAD, a lightweight universal interatomic potential for advanced materials modeling" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-mazitov2025 .

