# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Review first: the four comparison models of Table I (28 energy|force pairs, kept in the result comments) are not linked to registry models. The paper describes MACE-MP-0-L with about 15.8M parameters and MatterSim-5M with 4.6M parameters trained on 17M structures, while the registry rows say 5.7M parameters for MACE-MP-0 L=2 (2024-01-07) and 'about 6M training structures' for MatterSim-v1; until those descriptions are reconciled the identity is not certain. Orb-v2 and SevenNet-l3i5 are not in the registry.
# - Table I benchmarks are subsets recomputed with the MAD (PBEsol) settings, as the paper explains in its methods; the errors of models trained on PBE data therefore include the change of functional. The row labelled MAD is taken as the MAD test split.
# - PET is registered as a method with this paper as its first use in the KG; the method was introduced earlier (Pozdnyakov and Ceriotti, 2023). numFeatures holds the token size (256); batchSize is per GPU (24 on each of 8 GPUs). trainingDuration is the stated 'about 40 hours'.
# - Not encoded: LoRA fine-tuned and bespoke PET models for the six applications (Li thiophosphate conductivity, GaAs melting, HEA surface segregation, quantum nuclear effects in water and NMR, BaTiO3 dielectric response), the uncertainty-quantification scheme, the direct-force head and timings. Read from the arXiv v2 preprint; arXiv id matched by title and author.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
